-- Regression fixture for issue #920, for a name that is not in scope at all
-- (a misspelt or undeclared type) rather than an ambiguous one.
--
-- `Money` is never declared, so the ONE error the user should see is that it
-- cannot be found.
--
-- What used to happen instead: resolution handed back an `OutOfScope` sentinel
-- with an unregistered unique, and checking the body against it produced two
-- more diagnostics -- an accusation that "this is an error in this system and
-- should be reported as a bug", and a type mismatch between NUMBER and `Money`
-- that only restates the first error.
--
-- The golden for this file must therefore contain exactly the one error.

GIVEN amount IS A Money
GIVETH A NUMBER
`total due` MEANS amount
